From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 21:49:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Buffer tool evidence from unverified students and flush it on
 verification

A student is only VERIFIED once the Google Form warm-up is SUBMITTED - opening
it does nothing, typing answers does nothing. Until then studentId is empty and
reportToolResult dropped every result they produced. Not an edge case: a late
arrival, anyone who never presses submit, any Apps Script hiccup. They worked
the manipulative all period and the proficiency spine saw nothing.

- Unverified devices buffer each result to localStorage (bounded at 300)
  instead of discarding it. Nothing UNATTRIBUTED is ever written to the server,
  so the privacy posture is unchanged - the work waits on the device.
- flushPendingToolResults posts the buffer the instant saveVerifiedStudentJoin
  completes, so submitting the warm-up at minute 40 files the whole period. It
  also retries on each poll tick, so a verification that landed during a network
  blip is not stranded until tomorrow.
- A partial flush keeps what did not send rather than dropping the remainder.
- If a student never verifies, nothing lands. That is the honest outcome, and it
  is what a teacher-visible unverified count is for.

Also fixed: the day tally was keyed by studentId, so a student who verified
mid-lesson started a fresh tally and silently discarded every attempt made
before submitting the warm-up. Keyed by session now, which is what a per-device
tally actually represents.

